{
  "out": "/tmp/photonz-playtest/words-that-grow-move-as-one-walk",
  "seed": "Words that grow in a video move as one solid piece (the user, 2026-11-24: the individual characters jitter by a pixel or two independently). At Next defaults with no flag changed: a blank black video, a title typed on it, its letters set loose so they can be told apart, Scale keyed from 50 to 100 over a second. Every letter is followed in the pictures the canvas is handed as it plays and in the export's frames: none may slip against the rest by a tenth of a pixel and the word may never step backwards.",
